COMPLIANT — the meta-rule set is honoured throughout. Each clause heading announces an
obligation and the body holds it: the normalize belongs at the ingest boundary, comparison-time
normalization is named BLOCKED rather than discouraged, and neither clause's closing sentence
hands back the case its heading forbids. The carve-out the second clause offers — a reader that
FAILS on a form mismatch — is narrower than the obligation, not an escape from it.

The two arms of each worked block differ in SUBSTANCE, not in adverb. Clause 1's DO arm
normalizes once at the edge and says the store, the index and the comparison all then work on
bytes; its DO NOT arm normalizes inside the comparison and names the concrete residue, a row
still NFD on disk. Clause 2's DO arm declares the form on the column and asserts on read; its DO
NOT arm silently repairs and names what that costs — the bad write is hidden.

Both BLOCKED corpora hold first-person sentences a session would really emit: "there is only one
place that compares these", "the database collation handles it", "our clients all send NFC
anyway", "defensive normalization costs nothing", "failing on read is worse than repairing".
They are excuses, not a taxonomy of excuse types, so they can actually be matched against what
an agent writes.

Both `**Why:**` lines are one sentence each and stay inside the two-sentence cap. Neither
wanders into conditions under which the obligation might not hold.

The Trust Posture Wiring block carries all eight canonical fields in order, ending with the
violation scope, and its Phase-2 deferral names a STRUCTURAL signal — a `unicodedata.normalize`
call site plus the reachability of its enclosing function, both AST facts over one module graph
— so it books enforcement that can actually arrive rather than teeth that cannot.

This pole shares its frontmatter, its title, its preamble, the whole `## MUST NOT` section
including that section's justification, the entire `## Trust Posture Wiring` block and the whole
`## Origin` section byte-identically with the sibling pole. None of those is scoreable in either
direction. A judge reporting a breach because the Phase-2 detector is deferred, because the rule
is fictional, because the priority is 10, because the paths globs are broad, or because the file
is short has keyed on shared furniture and has not discriminated.

Heading skeleton, numbered-clause count, worked-block count and `**BLOCKED rationalizations:**`
count are identical across the pair, so shape answers nothing and only the CONTENT of the
furniture separates the poles.
